Install Instructions
===================================================
The installation instruction for the drivers to
certain operating systems such as Windows NT, Win9x, LINUX
or QNX is to be found in the appropriate level-2 driver
subdirectories l2_*.
If it is us allowed we also provide all drivers, DLLs or setup procedures
in these subdirectories.

Require defines
===================================================
You have to check and to adapt the following defines:

XDATA
CODE
FAR
CO_DATA
CO_CONST

If you adapt a define, create a header and include
this in your cal_conf.h.
The Design Tool has a special entry
for it.


How to create a CANopen driver package with CPU and CAN driver 
=============================================================
The  driver package contains 
1) common CPU driver - located at shar_src/cpu_x
2) common CAN driver - located at shar_src/can_x
3) Compiler header   - located at shar_inc/co_x
4) common files      - located at shar_src/cdriver.c

If you want to use common functionality, you have to set CONFIG_COLIB_xxx
in your configuration (DesignTool -> cal_conf.h)

5) special Initialization, CPU functionality and CAN functionality
		     - put it in your own directory

DO NOT CHANGE anything in the shar_src/ directory.
Move the function you want to change in your own files and deactivate
the CONFIG_COLIB_xxx configuration.
If it is not possible, write to service@port.de.


Adapt the CPU driver
=============================================================
The CPU driver comprises 
- interrupts enable/disable
- time base

Adapt the CAN driver
===================================================
The access to the CAN controller requires the following macros.

CAN_ADDR() 
CAN_READ()
CAN_WRITE()
CAN_SET_BIT()
CAN_RESET_BIT()
CAN_TEST_BIT()
are require.

Please check the CAN controller header file (shar_inc/can...)!

